WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.370
The biggest task in learning a language
is acquiring words. You need a lot of

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:10.920
words. At first you need some of the key
words so that you can say something, and

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:16.020
so that you can understand simple
content in the language. But in the long

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:21.960
run, you're going to have to learn a lot
of words. LingQ makes that easy. Trying to

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.970
learn words from a list doesn't work.
LingQ helps you learn words from a

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:32.030
context, from a meaningful context, so
just simply follow the instructions,

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:37.440
convert the blue words to yellow words,
save them. Don't worry about whether you

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.920
can remember them, you're gonna forget
them, I always forget them, and you'll

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.450
meet them again as yellow words, but just
simply work your way through the content

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:51.660
creating as many LingQs as you can, saving
words so that the known words total and

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:56.370
your LingQs total increases, and that's an
indication that you are on your way to

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.719
learning the language.

